28:     """
29:     Fill each vertical foreground band's background cells with the color of the next band to its right.
30: 
31:     Input structure
32:     - The dominant color is the background.
33:     - Each other color occupies a separate vertical band defined by that color's
34:       minimum and maximum columns.
35:     - Within a band, all cells are either that band's color or background.
36: 
37:     Rule
38:     - Order the bands from left to right.
39:     - In each band, replace background pixels with the color of the next band in
40:       that order, wrapping from the rightmost band back to the leftmost.
41:     - Preserve all existing foreground pixels and all background pixels outside
42:       the bands.
43: 
44:     Key insight
45:     - The column bands form a cyclic palette legend: a band's gaps are completed
46:       by borrowing the color from its right-hand neighbor, not by changing the
47:       band's existing pixels.
48:     """
